<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ngāi Tahu</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kāi Tahu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ngāi Tahu is the principal Māori iwi, or tribe, of the South Island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>, whose territory covers most of the island. Its claims over land purchases by the Crown in the nineteenth century were pursued for more than a century, and the settlement of 1998 brought a Crown apology and financial redress. Its commercial arm has since become one of the largest businesses in the South Island.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ngai-tahu.jpg" alt="Ngāi Tahu" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Igover · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ng%C4%81i_Tahu_Takiwa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
